.SH "NAME"
pcre2_callout_enumerate \- enumerate callouts in a compiled pattern
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

int\fP \f(CBpcre2_callout_enumerate\fP\f(CR(
      const pcre2_code *\fP\f(CIcode\fP\f(CR,
      int (*\fP\f(CIcallback\fP\f(CR)(pcre2_callout_enumerate_block *\fP\f(CIcallout_block\fP\f(CR,
                      void *\fP\f(CIcallout_data\fP\f(CR),
      void *\fP\f(CIcallout_data\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function scans a compiled regular expression and calls the \f(CBcallback\fP\f(CR()\fP
function for each callout within the pattern. The yield of the function is zero
for success and non\-zero otherwise. The arguments are:
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 13
\f(CIcode\fP
.ad l
Points to the compiled pattern
.TP 13
\f(CIcallback\fP
.ad l
The callback function
.TP 13
\f(CIcallout_data\fP
.ad l
User data that is passed to the callback
.PD
.RE
.PP
.ad l
.sp
The \f(CBcallback\fP\f(CR()\fP function is passed a pointer to a data block containing
the following fields (not necessarily in this order):
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CRuint32_t\fP \f(CIversion\fP\f(CR;\fP\&                 \f(CI/* Block version number */\fP
\f(CRuint32_t\fP \f(CIcallout_number\fP\f(CR;\fP\&          \f(CI/* Number for numbered callouts */\fP
\f(CRPCRE2_SIZE\fP \f(CIpattern_position\fP\f(CR;\fP\&      \f(CI/* Offset to next item in pattern */\fP
\f(CRPCRE2_SIZE\fP \f(CInext_item_length\fP\f(CR;\fP\&      \f(CI/* Length of next item in pattern */\fP
\f(CRPCRE2_SIZE\fP \f(CIcallout_string_offset\fP\f(CR;\fP \f(CI/* Offset to string within pattern */\fP
\f(CRPCRE2_SIZE\fP \f(CIcallout_string_length\fP\f(CR;\fP \f(CI/* Length of callout string */\fP
\f(CRPCRE2_SPTR\fP \f(CIcallout_string\fP\f(CR;\fP\&        \f(CI/* Points to callout string or is
                                     NULL */\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.sp
The second argument passed to the \f(CBcallback\fP\f(CR()\fP function is the callout data
that was passed to \f(CBpcre2_callout_enumerate()\fP. The \f(CBcallback\fP\f(CR()\fP
function must return zero for success. Any other value causes the pattern scan
to stop, with the value being passed back as the result of
\f(CBpcre2_callout_enumerate()\fP.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.